  "base": "e49b052",
  "claims": [
    "P2.1: a checkout only behind its upstream delivers the upstream's files, the receipt records the upstream commit, and the checkout's HEAD, branch and git status are unchanged.",
    "P2.2: a checkout behind with commits or uncommitted changes of its own under skills, agents, devtools or examples is delivered as it is, and the warning is printed before anything is written.",
    "P2.3 and P2.3b: level, ahead only, detached, no upstream, not a checkout, and an upstream configured with no ref each deliver the checkout, with no new line except the one warning for the missing upstream.",
    "P2.4 and P2.5: a fetch that fails or times out is a warning with exit 0; --as-is starts no git fetch.",
    "P2.6 and P2.7: compare reads the same files as apply; a source folder inside another repository is never fetched.",
    "S0.2: no command this phase adds changes the dev-tools checkout except git fetch, and no temporary folder is left behind.",
    "The phase 1 repairs (2120090) do what the phase-1-r1 ledger says, and standard output and exit codes of apply and check are as phase 1 left them."
  ],
